It is written from Espressif's public ESP-IDF headers and documentation and
from analysis of the RF test library (librftest.a) that ships with ESP-IDF.
At build time it links ESP-IDF (Apache-2.0) and Espressif's precompiled PHY,
Wi-Fi and RF test libraries, which are distributed by Espressif under their
own license terms and are not part of this repository.

The RTL-SDR driver (firmware/main/rtl_drv.c) is a C port of code from
webrtlsdr (https://github.com/jtarrio/webrtlsdr):
  Copyright 2013 Google Inc.
  Copyright 2024 Jacobo Tarrio Barreiro
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

The USB host stack is Espressif's espressif/usb component (Apache-2.0),
downloaded by the ESP-IDF component manager at build time.

The FM radio build also uses, downloaded the same way: espressif/esp_codec_dev
(Apache-2.0) for the audio codec, and espressif/esp-sr with its models for
voice commands, under the ESPRESSIF MIT License, which permits use on
Espressif products such as the ESP32-S31.
